0.5.1:
- [x] Add better automated QA process to prevent bugs

0.5.1a:
- [x] Include token input caching hits/misses in our message telemetry

0.5.1b:
- [x] Chat: honor a `?llm_model=` URL param on the chat page — pin the model picker to the requested model (validated against the real dropdown options) and persist it to the session `llmModel` cookie, so funnels that need an image-capable model (e.g. the mothership picture-to-html flow, where the default DeepSeek v4 Flash can't see images) can hand users off to Gemini 3 Flash instead of the image-blind default. Unknown keys are ignored and the param is stripped from the URL after load. Browser-smoke coverage added in Leonardo e2e.

0.5.1c:
- [x] Add the ability to do a Git Pull to receive updates from a different Leo instance (such as pulling changes from a dev instance into a prod instance). Adds a "check for updates" (cloud-arrow-down) button next to the existing push button in the History panel: it shows an "N updates available" badge when the box is behind its remote, a one-click "Update now" that does `git pull --ff-only` and restarts the llamapress container so the new code goes live, and a branch switcher to checkout+pull a different branch. Built for the two-VM workflow (push from a dev box, pull on prod) and kept dead-simple for non-technical operators. A fast-forward blocked by local edits surfaces a plain-language message ("you have file changes on this version that conflict… commit or discard them before pulling this update") instead of raw git output. New endpoints: GET /api/git/remote-status, POST /api/git/pull, POST /api/git/checkout (branch validated against the real remote list). pytest coverage in app/tests/test_git_pull.py.

0.5.1d:
- [x] Auto switch to image model Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite and back to non-image model, DeepSeek v4 if an image is uploaded.
- [x] Clear image attachment if switched to non-image model (middleware strip)

0.5.1e:
- [x] Bump LangChain version that supports way more efficient checkpoints that don't take up so much disk space. Adopted LangGraph **DeltaChannel** (beta, langgraph 1.2): the `messages` channel now stores an incremental delta per checkpoint + a periodic snapshot instead of re-serializing the whole message list every checkpoint (~O(N) storage instead of O(N^2) — LangChain benchmarks ~41x less). Stack bump (deliberate, together): langgraph 1.2.2→1.2.5 (DeltaChannel correctness fixes), langgraph-checkpoint-postgres 3.0.4→3.1.0 (delta-aware saver), langgraph-sdk 0.3.6→0.4.2, langchain-core 1.4.6→1.4.7, orjson 3.10.18→3.11.9 (resolution verified clean). Opted the whole RailsAgentState fleet + the llamabot agent into DeltaChannel via a shared `messages` annotation (`app/agents/utils/delta_state.py`). Reworked `checkpoint_cleanup.py`: the old aggressive "keep only the latest checkpoint" trim would destroy a delta chain (reconstruction replays ancestor writes back to the nearest snapshot), so post-run cleanup is now gated on `graph_uses_delta_channel(app)` — skipped for delta agents (history retained cheaply, which also restores continue/time-travel), kept for legacy non-delta agents; the periodic sweep is now orphan-only (deletes only writes/blobs with no surviving parent checkpoint). Coverage in `app/tests/test_checkpoint_cleanup_delta.py`.
